  NOTES
  ─────
  - Dataset: 150 labeled tweets (50 real Musashi feed + 100 synthetic traps).
  - Snapshot: 79 frozen markets across crypto, politics, sports, finance,
    geopolitics, breaking news.
  - The "~" on baseline TPs reflects that I did not save the baseline TP/FN
    breakdown to disk before applying the fixes; only the FP and F1 numbers
    were captured at each fix step.
  - "Temporal drift" on the final keyword row: the matcher scores markets
    partly by recency (markets ending soon score higher), so the same code
    produces slightly different numbers as the snapshot ages. Final keyword
    F1 drifted from 0.256 → 0.278 between June 5 and June 10 with no code
    change. Not a bug — just a property of the eval setup.

